# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 738 slice 2: a path through a captured Structure past its field (`loc\box\c`, value position) --
# slice 1 copies value fields one level deep.  The model is tried for the walk silently; its host said only "a callable merge needs a walkable body" at its
# header, and the model's own reason, where it stands, was lost (steps/capture-738.md §5, "Остаётся").
Inner:
    int: c 5
end: Inner

Model:
    int: other 5
    Inner: box
    int: count 0
    int: value 0
end: Model

fn: probe (Inner: q) int
    return: q\c

fn: makeReader (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    loc: merge: Model
    loc\value: n
    fn: read (int: x) int
        return: loc\box\c + x
    return: read

@: r40 makeReader(40)
int: a (r40: 2)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
